  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an N×MN\\times MN×M grid, with each cell initially painted white.\n\nYou need to paint exactly KKK of these cells black, such that every black cell is reachable from every other black cell, by travelling horizontally, vertically or diagonally through other black cells.\n\nFind the number of ways to paint the grid in such a manner, modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case contains a single line of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains three space-separated integers NNN, MMM and KKK — the number of rows, columns in the grid, and the number of cells to be painted black respectively.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of ways to paint the grid in such a manner, modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤M≤1051 \\leq M \\leq 10^51≤M≤105",
      "The summation of N⋅MN\\cdot MN⋅M over all testcases does not exceed 10510^5105",
      "1≤K≤min(6,N⋅M)1 \\leq K \\leq min(6, N\\cdot M)1≤K≤min(6,N⋅M)"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5\n2 2 3\n6 1 6\n6 6 6\n123 111 4\n7 7 1",
        "output": "4\n1\n31992\n1451221\n49",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: There are only 444 valid colorings.\nIn each valid coloring, exactly one of the 444 corners of the grid is uncolored.\nTest case 222: The only valid coloring is to color the whole grid."
      }
    ]
  },
